  "prompt": "You are a senior equity research associate at a global investment bank's technology sector coverage team. Your managing director has asked you to prepare a comprehensive investment memorandum on Alphabet Inc. (GOOGL) for an upcoming client pitch meeting with a large institutional investor seeking to evaluate a potential long position in mega-cap technology equities. The client is particularly interested in Alphabet's recent financial trajectory, capital allocation efficiency, and growth sustainability relative to the broader internet sector. Your analysis will directly inform the client's allocation decision.\n\nMaterials Provided:\n- Alphabet Inc. financial data extracted from recent SEC filings (10-K and 10-Q), including quarterly and annual revenue, operating income, net income, total assets, liabilities, stockholders' equity, cash and cash equivalents, diluted EPS, and R&D expense data spanning FY2024 through Q1 2026.\n- A list of Alphabet's recent SEC filings from May 2026.\n\nTask Requirements:\nPrepare an investment memorandum in PDF format titled 'Investment Memo - Alphabet Inc.' that includes the following sections:\n\n1. Executive Summary: Provide a concise investment thesis summarizing Alphabet's financial position, key growth drivers, and primary risk factors. State a clear recommendation (e.g., Overweight, Neutral, Underweight) with supporting rationale.\n\n2. Company Overview: Describe Alphabet's core business operations and competitive positioning in the technology and internet sector. Reference the company's CIK number and sector classification.\n\n3. Financial Performance Analysis: Analyze Alphabet's revenue growth trajectory from FY2024 through Q1 2026. Calculate and present year-over-year revenue growth rates for available periods. Analyze operating income margins (operating income as a percentage of revenue) for FY2025 and Q1 2026. Evaluate net income trends and diluted EPS progression.\n\n4. Balance Sheet Assessment: Examine Alphabet's asset growth, leverage ratios (total liabilities to total assets), and equity base expansion from FY2025 to Q1 2026. Analyze the change in cash and cash equivalents over the same period.\n\n5. R&D Investment and Innovation: Assess Alphabet's R&D spending as a percentage of revenue for FY2025 and Q1 2026. Discuss the implications of sustained R&D intensity for long-term competitive positioning.\n\n6. Risk Factors: Identify and discuss at least three material financial or operational risks evident from the data, including concentration risks, margin pressures, or capital allocation concerns.\n\n7. Conclusion and Recommendation: Reiterate the investment thesis and provide a 12-month price target rationale based on the financial metrics analyzed.\n\nConstraints:\n- All financial figures must be sourced from the provided data. Do not invent or assume data points.\n- Focus analysis on the most recent available periods: FY2024, FY2025, and Q1 2026.\n- The memo should be 6-10 pages in length (excluding exhibits).\n- Include at least one data table summarizing key financial metrics.\n- Use professional investment banking formatting with clear section headings.",
